course: dictionary
lesson: 8784
title: Shame: a feeling and a word
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Shame is a bad, hot feeling inside you when you know you did something wrong or silly and others may know. Read the words around it to find out which meaning is used. «Shame again, and a second confession.» Here the child has done wrong and owns up to it twice, so shame is the bad feeling.
explain: Shame can also mean a pity. «It's a shame it rained» means that is sad, not that anyone did anything bad. If nobody did anything wrong, shame probably just means it is a pity.
explain: Shame can be a verb too. To shame someone is to make them feel bad or embarrassed, often in front of others. In Kipling's tale, Balkis helps so that the wife believes her husband, and he is not shamed. The shaming is something done to a person.
explain: We should never use shame to hurt others. A child who is hurt or tricked has nothing to be ashamed of. Owning up often makes shame go away.
fact: Shame means the bad feeling you have when you know you did something wrong or silly.
fact: «It's a shame» or «what a shame» means it is sad or a pity.
fact: To shame someone is to make them feel bad or embarrassed, often in front of others.
fact: «Shame on you» is a way of telling someone they behaved badly.
fact: Shame is a noun (a shame, uncountable) and a verb (shames, shamed, shaming).
exercise: «The shame was worse than before.» What does shame mean here? | * A bad feeling after doing something wrong, made worse by hiding it | To make someone laugh | A pity, so it is sad | A bad feeling after doing something wrong
exercise: «It's a shame it rained.» What does shame mean here? | * A pity, so that is sad | A bad feeling after doing something wrong | To make someone else feel bad | A loud shout
exercise: In Kipling's tale, Balkis helps so that the Butterfly's wife believes him and «he is not shamed». What does shamed mean here? | Made to laugh at his own boasting | Given a prize | * Made to feel bad or embarrassed
test: «Shame again, and a second confession.» What does shame mean here? | Being happy | A pity | * The bad feeling of having done something wrong | A loud noise
test: Which sentence uses shame as a verb? | * «Balkis helps so that he is not shamed» | «The shame was worse than before» | «It's a shame it rained» | «Shame on you»
exam: «Shame on you» means | You won a prize | Please come here | It's a pity | * You behaved badly
